#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD9719 expect=skipped domain=DS
#note "The inherited DS answer: PMDA-SD0021's own Domains.Exclude already lists DS (with AG/BE/DE/DT/DV/ML), and the sister carries the parent's scope, so no extra entry was needed on this arm - unlike the FDA twin, whose parent has no exclusion list. Violating-shaped (no end/dur/occur/stat columns) to prove ONLY the exclusion silences."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | COMPLETED | COMPLETED
